# Ship Workflow

Every change follows three stages in order. Do not skip ahead, and do not
report a change as done before stage 3 passes.

## 1. Verify locally

```bash
npm run health          # is the dev server up? distinguishes "down" from "broken"
npm run dev:bg          # start it detached if health says it is down
npm run build           # types + lint + production build
npm run verify:model    # projection math
npm run verify          # full browser suite against localhost:3000
```

A green `npm run build` is **not** evidence the app works. It has given a false
all-clear before. Only the browser suite counts.

## 2. Commit and push

Commit in small focused increments as you go, never in one batch at the end —
agent processes in this project have died mid-task and lost uncommitted work.

Never commit `.playwright-browsers/`, `.next*/`, or any file over ~50 MB.
A 227 MB Chromium binary once had to be stripped by rewriting history.

## 3. Validate the hosted site

Pushing to `main` auto-deploys to https://nil68657.github.io/make-money-last/

```bash
export GH_TOKEN=$(gh auth token)   # `gh auth status` falsely reports logged out
gh run watch                       # wait for the deploy to finish
npm run verify:live                # browser suite against the live URL
```

A green Actions run only means the build succeeded. It does not mean the site
works — a broken `basePath` deploys "successfully" and renders unstyled or
blank. Confirm the live page serves styled content with `_next/` assets
resolving, then exercise the real flow: pick two cities, Calculate, see results.

If the live check fails, fix forward and redeploy. Never leave `main` broken.
